  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening GBV services for vulnerable women and girls in affected districts by El Nino drought-impact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the UNFPA project is to strengthen Gender-Based Violence (GBV) services for vulnerable women and girls in districts affected by the El Nino drought impact. UNFPA, with its implementing partners, establishes 40 safe spaces to provide psychosocial support for the most vulnerable women and girls. The project increases accessibility to survivor-centered GBV life-saving multi-sectoral services and enhance community awareness of Gender-Based Violence in Emergencies (GBViE). This project provides life-saving assistance to 32,000 people, of whom 14,879 women, 5,910 men and 11,211 children. An estimated 2,880 people with disabilities benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
